          "Type": "CloudFormation Security Check",
          "ID": "AWS-0013",
          "Title": "CloudFront distribution uses outdated SSL/TLS protocols.",
          "Description": "You should not use outdated/insecure TLS versions for encryption. You should be using the latest TLS policies available.\nNote: that setting *minimum_protocol_version = \"TLSv1.X\"* is only possible when *cloudfront_default_certificate* is false (eg. you are not using the cloudfront.net domain name).\nIf *cloudfront_default_certificate* is true then the Cloudfront API will only allow setting *minimum_protocol_version = \"TLSv1\"*, and setting it to any other value will result in a perpetual diff in your *terraform plan*'s.\nThe only option when using the cloudfront.net domain name is to ignore this rule.\n",
          "Message": "Distribution uses an insecure minimum TLS protocol version.",
          "Namespace": "builtin.aws.cloudfront.aws0013",
          "Query": "data.builtin.aws.cloudfront.aws0013.deny",
